<ArticleLayout slug="europe-campaign-localization" ctaLabel="Send a brief" faq={faq}>
  <p class="standfirst">Translation is the smallest job. Take one campaign into France, Germany, Spain and Italy and the discount, the green line, the image labels and the sale dates all get rechecked, market by market. The formats stay exactly as they are.</p>

  <h2>What changes in campaign localization for Europe?</h2>

  <p>Campaign localization in Europe changes four things before it touches the copy: how a discount shows its old price, whether a sustainability line survives, which retouching or AI labels the images carry, and when a sale may run. The formats do not change. hubStudio describes production practice here, not legal advice.</p>

  <p>Take one campaign with four parts: a hero image with a model, a 9:16 video, a "30 percent off" promotion and a line that says "eco-friendly packaging." Here is what each market asks of it.</p>

